     [4]
        Logistic regression is a statistical model widely used for classification problems, mainly
for binary classification . It linearly combines features and uses the Sigmoid function to map
the result to a probability value between 0 and 1 to address binary classification issues. The
model uses maximum likelihood estimation to optimize parameters and interprets the impact
of features on the probability of an event occurring through regression coefficients.
